{"id":1380,"level":64,"name":"Рокіровка (1)","group":"Правила","format":30,"description":"Castling is a special type of move.<br />It is the only way in chess to move two pieces in the same move: the king and a rook.<br />Castling is done to move the king to a safer place.<br />It also makes it easier to get the rook into the game. <p>There are two types of castling: short and long.<br />One rook is closer to the king than the other.<br />Short castling is done with the rook closest to the king.<br />Long castling involves the far rook.<br />In both cases, the king moves two squares sideways. To the left or to the right.<br />The rook jumps over the king. It comes to stand on the square right next to the king.<br />You do this in one single move!</p> <p>In example 1, both players castle short (to the right).<br />In example 2, both players castle long (to the left).</p> <p>Castling is not always allowed. You may NOT castle when<br />1. Either the king or the rook has already moved before.<br />2. The squares between the king and the rook are not empty.<br />3. The king is in check.<br />4. The king jumps over a square that is being attacked. The king may not move &lsquo;through&rsquo; check.<br />5. The king moves into check by castling.</p> <p><strong>What do you have to do?</strong><br />White wants to castle. Is he allowed to do so?<br />Click on the traffic lights to answer. Red = no, green = yes.</p>","assignment":"","stickerID":24,"examples":[{"fen":"4k1nr/5ppp/8/4p3/4P3/8/5PPP/4K1NR w Kk - 0 1","pgn":"1. Nf3 Nf6 2. O-O O-O *","text":"","format":30},{"fen":"rnb1k3/ppp5/8/3p4/3P4/8/PPP5/RNB1K3 w Qq - 0 1","pgn":"1. Nc3 Nc6 2. Be3 Bd7 3. O-O-O O-O-O *","text":"","format":30},{"fen":"5k2/5p1p/8/8/1b6/8/5PPP/4K2R w K - 0 1","pgn":"{[%cal Rb4e1]} 1. Ke2  *","text":"","format":30},{"fen":"5k2/5p1p/8/8/2b5/8/5PPP/4K2R w K - 0 1","pgn":"1. Kd2 {[%cal Rc4f1]} *","text":"","format":30},{"fen":"5k2/5p1p/8/8/3b4/8/6PP/4K2R w K - 0 1","pgn":"1. Ke2 {[%cal Rd4g1]} *","text"